<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Aliyu Babba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1894">1894</a>–<a href="/years/1903">1903</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Aliyu dan Abdullahi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Aliyu Babba was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kano">Kano</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a> from 1894 to 1903. He came to power after winning a civil war over the succession, and ruled as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sokoto-caliphate">Sokoto Caliphate</a>. After British forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-lugard">Frederick Lugard</a> captured Kano in February 1903 he was deposed and exiled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lokoja">Lokoja</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/aliyu-babba.jpg" alt="Aliyu Babba" width="320" height="395" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: D. J. M. Muffett · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emir_Aliyu_of_Kano.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
